Got everything I need. Here's your Tuesday check-in, Reuben.

---

**Rest day. Use it well.**

Today's a hard off day — and with Training Readiness sitting at 68 and only 6h31m of sleep last night, that's not a bad thing. You woke up with a Body Battery of 96, which means your body recovered from Monday's run well. Don't waste that by going into tomorrow's session under-slept.

---

**What the last 48 hours tell me:**

Monday's 7.18km was exactly right — 7:13/km, avg HR 126, never forced it past 143 max. That's the discipline this base phase demands. You didn't hero it, you executed it. Respect.

Saturday's 11.65km long run was solid too — 8:08/km, HR 128, aerobic training effect 2.8. Your body is responding.

July mileage: **31.7km through July 6.** You need ~100km this month. That's ~68km across the remaining ~25 days. Completely doable if you hit your scheduled runs — but there's no room to skip sessions.

---

**Tomorrow is the one that counts this week:**

Wednesday (Jul 8) — first quality session of July:
> 9km total: **2km easy warm-up → 5km tempo at 6:00–6:15/km (HR 155–165) → 2km cool-down**

This is where we start closing that 13–18 minute gap to your 1:45–1:50 goal. Current HM prediction is 2:03:15. You've got 12 weeks to fix that. Tempo discipline tomorrow starts that process.

Run it **before 7am.** Singapore heat is not negotiable.

---

**One thing for today:** Get 7.5+ hours tonight. Your HRV weekly avg is 69ms and rHR came in at 47 — your body is primed. Don't squander it with a short night.

Thursday is off too (hard constraint), so Wednesday's session stands alone this week. Make it count.
